    "value": "Liquibase pull request #2285 was submitted to address compatibility issues and vulnerabilities related to the H2 database upgrade from version 1.4.200 to 2.0.202. The need for this update arose due to a critical security vulnerability (CVE-2021-23463), and the update included necessary fixes for breaking changes introduced by H2 2.0.x.\n\nKey details:\n- The upgrade caused backward-incompatible issues, particularly around how Liquibase interacts with H2's INFORMATION_SCHEMA and the handling of auto-increment columns (e.g., the \"AUTO_INCREMENT\" syntax is no longer supported in the same way and should use \"IDENTITY\" instead in some cases).\n- PR #2285 (\"Bump h2 from 1.4.200 to 2.0.202 in /liquibase-dist\") was implemented to resolve such issues and ensure Liquibase works with H2 2.0.202【3:0†source】【3:6†source】.\n- The PR was motivated both by user reports of exceptions with auto-generated columns and by security scanner reports flagging the old H2 version as vulnerable.\n\nSummary: If you're using recent Liquibase with H2, you should use at least version 2.0.202, and PR #2285 integrated this support/fix into Liquibase to adapt to the new H2 behaviors and schema changes. This was a notable change for both security and compatibility.\n\nIf you need technical details on migrating Liquibase scripts or configurations from H2 1.4.200 to 2.0.202, let me know!",
    "annotations": [
      {
        "text": "",
