393.     /**
394.      * Should the given database include the table name in the key?
395.      * Databases that need to include the table names are ones where unique constraint names do not have to be unique
396.      * within the schema.
397.      *
398.      * Currently only mysql is known to have non-unique constraint names.
399.      *
400.      * If this returns true, the database-specific query in {@link #listColumns(UniqueConstraint, Database, DatabaseSnapshot)} must include
401.      * a TABLE_NAME column in the results for {@link #getCacheKey(Map, Database)} to use.
402.      */
403.     protected boolean includeTableNameInCacheKey(Database database) {
404.         return database instanceof MySQLDatabase;
